1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,887
Good morning.

2
00:00:00,887 --> 00:00:01,313
Total Insurance.

3
00:00:01,313 --> 00:00:03,610
Judy speaking, how may I help you?

4
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:07,836
I recently shipped my belongings from overseas back here to Australia

5
00:00:07,836 --> 00:00:10,910
and I took out insurance with your company.

6
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:15,230
Some items were damaged during the move so I need to make a claim.

7
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:16,330
What do I have to do?

8
00:00:16,330 --> 00:00:20,250
Okay, well first I need to get a few details about this.

9
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:22,420
Can you give me your name please?

10
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:23,092
Yes.

11
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:25,110
It's Michael Alexander.

12
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:25,700
Okay.

13
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,060
And your address please?

14
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,560
My old address or my current one?

15
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:31,670
Your current one.

16
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:36,610
It's 24 Manly Street, Milperra near Sydney.

17
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:38,550
What was the suburb, sorry?

18
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:41,485
Milperra.

19
00:00:41,485 --> 00:00:44,420
M-I-L-P-E-R-R-A.

20
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:44,869
Right.

21
00:00:44,869 --> 00:00:45,318
Now,

22
00:00:45,318 --> 00:00:48,460
who was the shipping agent Mr Alexander?

23
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:51,200
You mean the company we used?

24
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:54,800
Yes, the company who packed everything up at the point of origin.

25
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,611
Oh, it was.., er...

26
00:00:57,611 --> 00:00:59,720
First Class Movers.

27
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:00,311
Okay...

28
00:01:00,311 --> 00:01:03,860
where were the goods shipped from?

29
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:04,273
China,

30
00:01:04,273 --> 00:01:09,640
but the ship came via Singapore and was there for about a week.

31
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:13,330
Don't worry, all of that information will be in the documentation.

32
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:14,482
Now, the dates.

33
00:01:14,482 --> 00:01:17,170
Do you know when the ship arrived?

34
00:01:17,170 --> 00:01:21,825
It left on the 1lth of October and got to Sydney on the 28th

35
00:01:21,825 --> 00:01:22,490
of November.

36
00:01:22,490 --> 00:01:22,963
Okay.

37
00:01:22,963 --> 00:01:25,328
I need one more thing.

38
00:01:25,328 --> 00:01:27,220
There's a reference number.

39
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:31,187
It should be in the top right-hand corner of the pink form they gave

40
00:01:31,187 --> 00:01:31,470
you.

41
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:34,549
Let me have a look.

42
00:01:34,549 --> 00:01:37,629
I have so many papers.

43
00:01:37,629 --> 00:01:40,092
Yes, here it is.

44
00:01:40,092 --> 00:01:41,940
It's 601 ACK.

45
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:42,710
Thanks.

46
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:47,012
I need to take down a few details of the actual damage over the

47
00:01:47,012 --> 00:01:49,470
phone before you put in a full report.

48
00:01:49,470 --> 00:01:53,460
Can you tell me how many items were damaged and what the damage was?

49
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:55,433
Yes, well four things actually.

50
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:57,800
I'll start with the big things.

51
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:02,370
My TV first of all.It's a large one.., very expensive.

52
00:02:02,370 --> 00:02:05,320
Our insurance doesn't cover electrical problems.

53
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,040
It isn't an electrical problem.

54
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:10,070
The screen has a huge crack in it so it's unusable.

55
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:10,870
I see.

56
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:14,070
Any idea of the price to repair it?

57
00:02:14,070 --> 00:02:14,363
No.

58
00:02:14,363 --> 00:02:16,710
Well, I don't think it can be repaired.

59
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:18,470
It will need a new one.

60
00:02:18,470 --> 00:02:18,780
Okay.

61
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:22,810
I'll make a note of that and we'll see what we can do.

62
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:24,670
Now, what was the second item?

63
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:28,490
The cabinet from the bathroom was damaged as well.

64
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:31,650
It's a lovely cabinet, we use it to keep our towels in.

65
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:33,700
And what is the extent of the damage?

66
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:37,999
Well, the back and the sides seem okay but the door has a huge

67
00:02:37,999 --> 00:02:38,920
hole in it.

68
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,207
It can't be repaired.

69
00:02:40,207 --> 00:02:42,460
I'm really not very happy about it.

70
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,840
And how much do you think it will cost to replace it?

71
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,295
Well,

72
00:02:45,295 --> 00:02:50,300
when I bought it last year I paid $125 for it.

73
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:56,133
But the one I've seen here in Sydney is a bit more expensive, it's

74
00:02:56,133 --> 00:02:56,550
$140.

75
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:56,866
Right,

76
00:02:56,866 --> 00:02:58,760
and what was the third item?

77
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,576
My dining room table.

78
00:03:00,576 --> 00:03:03,300
It's a lovely table from Indonesia.

79
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:08,278
It must have been very hot inside the container because one leg has completely

80
00:03:08,278 --> 00:03:09,700
split down the middle.

81
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:13,760
The top and the other three look okay thank goodness,

82
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,930
Any idea of the price to repair it?

83
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:19,951
Well, I had an estimate done on this actually because it is a very

84
00:03:19,951 --> 00:03:21,100
special table to us.

85
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,756
They quoted us $200,

86
00:03:22,756 --> 00:03:28,550
which is really pricey so I hope the insurance will cover the total cost.

87
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:30,475
I'm sure that will be fine.

88
00:03:30,475 --> 00:03:32,720
What was the last item, Mr Alexander?

89
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:37,804
Well, we have a lovely set of china plates and dishes, you know, with

90
00:03:37,804 --> 00:03:39,620
matching cups, saucers, the lot.

91
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:44,028
They were all in the one box which must have got dropped

92
00:03:44,028 --> 00:03:46,600
because some plates were broken - six actually.

93
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:49,350
And can you tell me the replacement value of these?

94
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:52,484
Well, it's hard to say because they were part of a set

95
00:03:52,484 --> 00:03:56,140
but they can be up to $10 each as it's such a good set.

96
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:56,560
Okay,

97
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,500
so that would be around $60 altogether?

98
00:03:59,500 --> 00:03:59,920
Yes,

99
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:00,760
that's right.

100
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,700
And is that all of the items?

101
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,076
Yes.

102
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:06,080
So what do I have to do now?
